addition='Coupling between the wheel body and adjacent loaded teeth is an established mechanism in transmission-error prediction, including three-dimensional finite-element treatments [43]. Analytical and finite-element studies in Chinese also relate profile modification, machining errors and load-sharing transitions [44]. More recent direct parameter studies examine how modification settings influence transmission error [45]. These precedents motivate a precise distinction: a forward influence or a synthesis for a prescribed response does not establish which unknown relief coordinates can be inferred from a centred measured response. Our coupled-contact result concerns invariance under fixed compliance, rather than a new physical coupling model.\n\n'
